From 0efff4d0e79418f583b94bf7670ad44eb8df7bad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:05:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] yblod-engine-vk: shaders without shaderInt64 (Raspberry
 Pi 5)

v3dv has no shaderInt64. Every shader is now also built as "<name>@noi64"
with DV_NO_INT64: dv_common.glsl's helpers do the 64-bit maths on
uvec2(low, high) words, bit-identical to int64. Devices without
shaderInt64 use those (DVVK_NO_INT64=1 forces them).

- The native SPIR-V is byte-identical to before (the rewrite is macros
  that expand to the original expressions).
- dvvk-int64-check: each helper against native int64 on 4M inputs
  (edge values mixed in) on any device with shaderInt64.
- On lavapipe the engine's output is identical native vs emulated (and
  with DVVK_NO_PUSH_DESCRIPTOR=1) on P7 FEL (MMR 64-bit LUT and polynomial
  chroma), P8.1 (single polynomial) and MMR single-layer (piecewise) clips.
---
